  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $A=\\left\\{5^{n}-4 n-1: n \\in N\\right\\}$ and\r\n$B=\\{16(n-1): n \\in N],$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KmYLh",
      "text": "$A=B$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KggLi",
      "text": "$A \\cap B=\\phi$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2KBJ",
      "text": "$A \\subseteq B$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cclUp",
      "text": "$B \\subseteq A$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$\\begin{aligned} A &=5^{n}-4 n-1=(1+4)^{n}-4 n-1 \\\\ &=\\left({ }^{n} C_{0}+{ }^{n} C_{1} \\times 4+{ }^{n} C_{2} \\times 4^{2}+\\ldots+{ }^{n} C_{n} \\times 4^{n}\\right) \\\\ &=4^{2}\\left({ }^{n} C_{2}+{ }^{n} C_{3} \\times 4+\\ldots+{ }^{n} C_{n} \\times 4^{n-2}\\right) \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\therefore$ A contains some multiples of 16 \r\nClearly, $B$ contains all multiples of 16 including $0 .$\r\n$A \\subseteq B$",
    "image": null
  },
